WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.669
I joined my family, who were safely inside Rockburg.

2
00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:07.414
With pounding hearts, we watched the giant snake's approach.

3
00:00:07.415 --> 00:00:10.349
"It's a boa constrictor!" I whispered.

4
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:16.413
The boys fired their guns, one right after another. I also fired and missed.

5
00:00:16.414 --> 00:00:21.037
Startled but unhurt, the snake glided into the nearby marsh.

6
00:00:21.038 --> 00:00:24.898
"No one is to leave the cave without my permission," I said sternly.

7
00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:27.662
"That is a very dangerous snake!"

8
00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:31.636
For three days we—and our animals—stayed inside.

9
00:00:31.637 --> 00:00:34.769
The ducks and geese were still out on the marsh.

10
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:39.174
I knew the snake must be lurking in the reeds because the birds were so restless.

11
00:00:39.175 --> 00:00:41.899
We were running out of hay for the animals.

12
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.176
I was debating what to do when I looked out and saw the snake approaching again.

13
00:00:46.177 --> 00:00:51.011
Grabbing my gun, I fired at the snake, and this time I did not miss.

14
00:00:51.012 --> 00:01:00.358
After this episode I decided to take my family to our farm at Woodlands.

15
00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:05.606
The boys were soon bored, so I said they could go on an expedition without me.

16
00:01:05.607 --> 00:01:08.519
I wanted to encourage their independence.

17
00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.029
"I'd rather stay here with you and Mother," said Ernest.

18
00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:17.392
"Not me," said little Franz. "I can't wait to go exploring!"

19
00:01:17.393 --> 00:01:20.105
I would have preferred to keep Franz with us.

20
00:01:20.106 --> 00:01:24.208
But I had made the offer to all the boys, so I couldn't withdraw it.

21
00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:27.177
In high spirits, the three boys rode off.

22
00:01:27.178 --> 00:01:31.184
All day I wondered about their adventures.

23
00:01:31.185 --> 00:01:34.934
At sunset they returned and joined us around the campfire.

24
00:01:34.935 --> 00:01:38.211
"We had a splendid ride!" said Jack.

25
00:01:38.212 --> 00:01:42.438
"We went all the way through the Gap!" said little Franz.

26
00:01:42.439 --> 00:01:47.246
He was talking about a narrow pass we'd previously found through the rocky hills.

27
00:01:47.247 --> 00:01:51.206
"They're forgetting the most important thing," Fritz said impatiently.

28
00:01:51.207 --> 00:01:54.479
"We drove a herd of antelope right through the Gap!

29
00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:59.617
The antelope are in our territory now. All ready for us to hunt or tame."

30
00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:03.562
"That's wonderful," I said. "But what's to keep them there, Fritz?"

31
00:02:03.563 --> 00:02:06.153
"We strung a line across the pass—"

32
00:02:06.154 --> 00:02:10.089
"And hung feathers and rags from it," interrupted Franz.

33
00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:14.493
"Those things will dance in the wind and spook the antelope," explained Fritz.

34
00:02:14.494 --> 00:02:17.403
"I'm sure the herd won't try to go through the Gap."

35
00:02:17.404 --> 00:02:24.358
"Well done," I said. "Tomorrow I'd like to go out riding with you."

36
00:02:24.359 --> 00:02:29.249
The next day we rode to the Gap. I helped the boys to build a fence of bamboo.

37
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:33.280
"That ought to keep the antelope on our side of the Gap," I said.

38
00:02:33.281 --> 00:02:38.363
We were on our way back to Woodlands when Jack and Franz decided to gallop ahead.

39
00:02:38.364 --> 00:02:42.000
Suddenly four ostriches rose up from where they'd been resting.

40
00:02:42.001 --> 00:02:46.023
Jack brought down the large male ostrich with his lasso.

41
00:02:46.024 --> 00:02:49.838
We leaped from our steeds and tried to approach the captured bird.

42
00:02:49.839 --> 00:02:53.966
He kicked and struggled so hard that I feared we'd have to let him go.

43
00:02:53.967 --> 00:02:57.341
"If only we could block out the light," said Fritz.

44
00:02:57.342 --> 00:03:01.517
"Sometimes that calms birds—like putting a cover over a parrot's cage."

45
00:03:01.518 --> 00:03:05.241
I threw my coat over the bird's head, and he stopped struggling.

46
00:03:05.242 --> 00:03:08.562
"How are we going to get him home?" asked Jack.

47
00:03:08.563 --> 00:03:14.781
"I've heard it's possible to tame a wild elephant by making it walk between two tame elephants," I said.

48
00:03:14.782 --> 00:03:16.761
"Maybe that would work here."

49
00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:22.247
"But, Father, we don't have any tame ostriches," said little Franz.

50
00:03:22.248 --> 00:03:25.191
"We have Storm and Grumble," Jack pointed out.

51
00:03:25.192 --> 00:03:27.823
"I don't think they'll object to helping us."

52
00:03:27.824 --> 00:03:31.507
So we fastened the ostrich between the buffalo and the bull.

53
00:03:31.508 --> 00:03:34.074
Franz and Jack mounted their steeds.

54
00:03:34.075 --> 00:03:37.146
I removed my coat from the ostrich's head.

55
00:03:37.147 --> 00:03:40.266
For a few moments he lay perfectly still.

56
00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.972
Then he bounded up and tried to escape.

57
00:03:42.973 --> 00:03:46.328
But Storm and Grumble weren't about to let him do that.

58
00:03:46.329 --> 00:03:48.834
We slowly walked our prisoner home.

59
00:03:48.835 --> 00:03:53.688
As we approached, I could see the look of dismay on my wife's face.

60
00:03:53.689 --> 00:03:59.317
"See what we've got!" crowed little Franz. "An ostrich!"

61
00:03:59.318 --> 00:04:02.636
"Another mouth to feed!" my wife exclaimed.

62
00:04:02.637 --> 00:04:05.468
"You've brought home a useless pet!"

63
00:04:05.469 --> 00:04:08.641
"He's not useless, Mother," protested Jack.

64
00:04:08.642 --> 00:04:10.565
"You should see how fast he runs.

65
00:04:10.566 --> 00:04:16.331
He'll be the fastest animal in our stables. Just wait and see."

66
00:04:16.332 --> 00:04:21.453
A month later the ostrich was completely tame. Jack named him Hurricane.

67
00:04:21.454 --> 00:04:24.224
I made a saddle and a special bridle.

68
00:04:24.225 --> 00:04:27.753
The reins were attached to flaps over the bird's eyes.

69
00:04:27.754 --> 00:04:31.647
With both flaps open, the bird galloped straight ahead.

70
00:04:31.648 --> 00:04:34.258
Cover his right eye and he turned left.

71
00:04:34.259 --> 00:04:39.363
Cover his left eye and he turned right. Cover both eyes and he stopped.

72
00:04:39.364 --> 00:04:43.602
Jack took him out for a ride, and the bird galloped away.

73
00:04:43.603 --> 00:04:48.179
"Forget Hurricane," Jack said breathlessly when they returned.

74
00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:53.956
"This bird's name should be Hurry."

